# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the value:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser, and it inlines
# them into the built bundle at build time. Never put a real secret in here —
# anything VITE_-prefixed is readable by anyone who opens the built site.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Web3Forms access key — https://web3forms.com
# Delivers submissions from the contact form to: 404solutions.business@gmail.com
#
# This key is public by design: it names the destination inbox and is meant to
# live in client-side code. It is not a credential. If it is ever abused,
# rotate it in the Web3Forms dashboard.
#
# Restart the dev server after changing this — Vite reads .env at startup.
VITE_WEB3FORMS_KEY=your-web3forms-access-key
